'''''Lepidium ruderale''''' is [[species]] of [[flowering plant]]s in the mustard or cabbage family, [[Brassicaceae]]. It is native to temperate [[Asia]] and northern and eastern [[Europe]].  It has also naturalized in southwestern Europe and [[North America]].<ref>{{PLANTS|id=LERU|taxon=Lepidium ruderale|accessdate=20 Dec 2011}}</ref> Its common names include '''roadside pepperweed''', '''narrow-leaved pepperwort''', '''narrow-leaf pepperwort''', and '''peppergrass'''.<ref>{{GRIN | accessdate=20 December 2011}}</ref>

